description: Raise RUST_MIN_STACK when running synth-core integration tests
alwaysApply: true
---

# Integration test stack size

`synth-core` integration tests (especially `engine_tests`) place a large
`SynthEngine` on the stack. The default Rust thread stack is too small and
aborts with a stack overflow / out-of-memory-for-stack failure.

Whenever you run `cargo test` that includes `synth-core` integration tests
(`--tests`, `--test engine_tests`, or `--workspace`), set:

```bash
RUST_MIN_STACK=16777216
```

Example:

```bash
RUST_MIN_STACK=16777216 cargo test -p synth-core --tests
RUST_MIN_STACK=16777216 cargo test --workspace
```

Do not treat a stack overflow in these tests as a product bug until the run
has been retried with `RUST_MIN_STACK` set. See the root `README.md`
Development section and `synth-core/README.md`.
